{"built":"2026-10-31T14:48:06.480Z","clade":"Aves","label":"birds","provisional":false,"decision":{"clade":"Aves","status":"confirmed","decided_by":"Amit Shenoy, project lead, in his own words to the hub: \"Sure do AVes\"","relayed_by":"hub session scienceclaw-03 to the holdout thread (scienceclaw-93)","decided_on":"2026-10-31","provisional_from":"2026-10-31T05:52:44.982Z","alternative_considered":"Mammalia","reasoning":["Aves was chosen knowing it is underpowered for the tests built so far: the held-out bird counts fall below the builders’ own pre-registered minimum sample sizes, so both examined tests read inconclusive.","Mammalia would have made 1 of 2 examined tests decisive, but the examined tests had already fitted on mammal rows, and one further completed test uses mammals only and would have been built entirely on held-out data; a switch now would have made those tests post hoc.","The choice was therefore a clean blind that cannot yet decide over a decisive-looking test on a contaminated design, and the clean blind was taken.","The finding this records is about the data, not the thread: the public trait and demographic tables cannot support a blind clade exam at the builders’ own minimum n for these laws. That is more useful to the next team than a decisive number from a compromised design."],"cost":{"examined_tests":["kimura-heterozygosity","hamilton-senescence"],"held_out_counts":[{"test":"kimura-heterozygosity","clade":"Aves","held_out_n":13,"builder_min_n":50,"verdict":"inconclusive"},{"test":"kimura-heterozygosity","clade":"Mammalia","held_out_n":40,"builder_min_n":50,"verdict":"inconclusive"},{"test":"hamilton-senescence","clade":"Aves","held_out_n":8,"builder_min_n":15,"verdict":"inconclusive"},{"test":"hamilton-senescence","clade":"Mammalia","held_out_n":20,"builder_min_n":15,"verdict":"mixed"}],"decisive_exams_by_clade":{"Aves":0,"Mammalia":1},"tests_post_hoc_if_mammalia":["kimura-heterozygosity","hamilton-senescence","thompson1917-ch16-13"],"mammal_only_tests":["thompson1917-ch16-13"]}},"first_frozen_at":"2026-10-31T05:52:44.982Z","previous_freeze":{"frozen_at":"2026-10-31T05:52:44.982Z","provisional":true,"exam_json_sha256":"06b797929a27fad5b7173dbaa0c2d9d297deea478a64b7a7935f85caec430360","roster_unchanged":true,"superseded_because":"clade confirmed; provisional flag cleared and the decision recorded"},"rule":["An organism is held out when the inventory's lineage puts it in class Aves (any rank: species, genus, family, order, or the class itself).","The rule is the class, not the list: a bird species that is not in the inventory is held out too.","A taxon above class rank that contains Aves (Animalia, Metazoa, Eumetazoa, Bilateria, Deuterostomia, Chordata, Vertebrata, Craniata, Gnathostomata, Osteichthyes, Sarcopterygii, Tetrapoda, Amniota, Sauropsida, Diapsida, Archosauria, Dinosauria, Theropoda) is excluded from both sides, because its data mixes them.","Everything else is available for building (train).","Genome-ready means the best NCBI assembly is chromosome-level or a complete genome. NCBI's reference flag alone is not enough, because it also marks scaffold-level and contig-level assemblies."],"rules_for_builders":["Do not fit, tune, select or sanity-check anything on data for a bird: no Aves rows from trait tables, genomes, occurrence counts, fossils, or claim texts that only Aves organisms support.","A claim test's planned_datasets may name a shared table (AnAge, EltonTraits, the Amniote database) only with the held-out class filtered out, and the filter must be in the committed analysis script.","The exam is run once, after building stops, on the frozen roster below. The roster’s SHA-256 is in CHECKSUMS.json; node holdout/make-split.mjs --verify checks it.","Reading this file is allowed. It names organisms, identifiers and which tables cover them; it contains no trait values."],"what_is_tested":"Each candidate law that a builder supports on training organisms is re-scored, by an assessor who did not build it, on the held-out species below, using the same pre-registered pass and fail criteria. A law counts as generalizing only if it passes here.","frozen_at":"2026-10-31T14:38:42.937Z","checksums":{"clade":"Aves","provisional":false,"decision":{"status":"confirmed","decided_by":"Amit Shenoy, project lead, in his own words to the hub: \"Sure do AVes\"","decided_on":"2026-10-31"},"inputs":{"organisms/merged/taxa.json":{"sha256":"ac23df282cda36e20063fe3bdb2bd0519c8d8a2cad2618f4d1180083155480a8","bytes":480067},"organisms/merged/datasets.json":{"sha256":"c00121bc96e727fc9cc547b55faf9523ed54cd88042f74c400106e944e35b2f3","bytes":1994139},"dashboard/genomes.cache.json":{"sha256":"117eef84636b8d2e05f32a1388672899cea98c9e63de729ed01513dfb612b366","bytes":53410},"docs/claims.json":{"sha256":"da6ba24af6efe5f0eafdc16790ec85947c4e14d71ea9609f5ce9f9f3f4fe8581","bytes":1063673}},"outputs":{"split.json":{"sha256":"d73dab71347e21e047ea2304b3ae669ed08b780b515aeba249097545246c0855","bytes":282269},"exam.json":{"sha256":"f59b7b8ca2bdee21960f6a773de60967bc5c2933ffc75ee9da64e089228f5c7e","bytes":36005},"holdout-taxa.csv":{"sha256":"f149873b96d8359a310d32ca55874b63e7547f1df04c856d5dfb9b95ed9dd134","bytes":16088}},"roster_sha256":"9c4499751d6fa58502e9959e23ead955b1338f2dc84eb5fa24a61548d89277c3","generator":"holdout/make-split.mjs","frozen_at":"2026-10-31T14:38:42.937Z","first_frozen_at":"2026-10-31T05:52:44.982Z","previous_freeze":{"frozen_at":"2026-10-31T05:52:44.982Z","provisional":true,"outputs":{"split.json":{"sha256":"1e57dabb9cb49dbf6dee0f007421d1d095cec86e4d1fe879e1ebde1166dea94a","bytes":279981},"exam.json":{"sha256":"06b797929a27fad5b7173dbaa0c2d9d297deea478a64b7a7935f85caec430360","bytes":33717},"holdout-taxa.csv":{"sha256":"f149873b96d8359a310d32ca55874b63e7547f1df04c856d5dfb9b95ed9dd134","bytes":16088}},"roster_sha256":"9c4499751d6fa58502e9959e23ead955b1338f2dc84eb5fa24a61548d89277c3","roster_unchanged":true,"superseded_because":"clade confirmed; provisional flag cleared 